Subject: arg: let --spec-type none override earlier --spec-type values

--spec-type appends to params.speculative.types on every occurrence so
comma/repeat usage can combine speculators. But that means a packaged
llamafile whose baked-in .args set "--spec-type draft-mtp" can never be
switched off from the CLI: "--spec-type none" just appends NONE, which
the enabled-configs bitmask ignores, and draft-mtp stays active. The
README documents "--spec-type none" as the off switch, and benchmarking
against a no-speculation baseline is impossible without it.

Make "none" reset the accumulated list instead of appending.
common_speculative_types_from_names() already collapses any list
containing "none" to exactly {NONE}, so:

  --spec-type none                          -> speculation disabled
  --spec-type none --spec-type ngram-simple -> exactly ngram-simple
                                               (replaces baked-in default)

Plain values keep the append-to-combine semantics.

diff --git a/common/arg.cpp b/common/arg.cpp
--- a/common/arg.cpp
+++ b/common/arg.cpp
@@ -3652,7 +3652,14 @@
         [](common_params & params, const std::string & value) {
             const auto types_str = string_split<std::string>(value, ',');
             auto types = common_speculative_types_from_names(types_str);
-            params.speculative.types.insert(params.speculative.types.end(), types.begin(), types.end());
+            // "none" resets the accumulated list so a CLI --spec-type none can
+            // disable a default baked into a llamafile's .args (which appends
+            // CLI args after the baked-in ones)
+            if (!types.empty() && types[0] == COMMON_SPECULATIVE_TYPE_NONE) {
+                params.speculative.types = std::move(types);
+            } else {
+                params.speculative.types.insert(params.speculative.types.end(), types.begin(), types.end());
+            }
         }
     ).set_spec().set_examples({LLAMA_EXAMPLE_SPECULATIVE, LLAMA_EXAMPLE_SERVER, LLAMA_EXAMPLE_CLI}).set_env("LLAMA_ARG_SPEC_TYPE"));
     add_opt(common_arg(
